{"kind":"request","text":"Planner files hugh direction of 2026-10-07 08:45 Eastern as design request R5, to the planners, held until gate 2 lands (plan 024). (1) A propose-from-branch command: artroom propose \u003cbranch\u003e takes the commits of a local branch and submits them as a change in the room (the change lane source entries carrying the pack and the manifest, the proposal act), so the room, not the person, publishes; it rests on gate 2 lane wiring (14db4e69) and the change lane reports field. (2) An offline and disconnected model: a client signs intents offline with the observations it holds, keeps an outbox, syncs in the background, and reconciles by replaying the scope histories; a stale intent is refused with its reason and the client re-bases it, as git rebases commits. State the rules for expected observations after long disconnection, pack sizes through the Worker (maxBytes), and one key per device. (3) The same shape as a generic optimistic local model for any room application: local projection, signed outbox, background propose and sync, refusal as rollback, so the experience is responsive without the room losing its judgment. (4) Creation not linked to GitHub: a second host adapter on the Git hosting the Worker runs beside (the old spike used it), so a repository made only here is cloned, pulled and proposed to the same way. Not before the demo gates.","body":{"conditions":"A design note in the dev-onboarding form (nouns, verbs, invariants) covering the propose-from-branch command, the offline and disconnected model, the optimistic local model for room applications and creation on a second host adapter, with one request per gate it depends on; filed after gate 2 lands.","design":"R5-offline","held_until":"gate-2-landed","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}